From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: serial: base: preserve console TX on hangup

Do not disable TX when hanging up a console port. When procd's
askconsole fork calls TIOCSCTTY with force=1 the kernel hangs up the
previous session, which triggers uart_hangup() -> uart_shutdown() ->
serial_port_set_tx(false). Stopping TX silences all subsequent kernel
console output permanently.

uart_hangup() already skips uart_change_pm(PM_OFF) for console ports;
apply the same guard here.

Signed-off-by: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_port.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_port.c
@@ -110,7 +110,16 @@
 {
 	struct serial_port_device *port_dev = port->port_dev;

-	serial_base_port_set_tx(port, port_dev, false);
+	/*
+	 * Do not disable TX on a console port. When procd's askconsole fork
+	 * calls TIOCSCTTY with force=1, the kernel hangs up the previous
+	 * session, triggering uart_hangup() -> uart_shutdown() -> here.
+	 * Stopping TX kills all kernel console output permanently.
+	 * uart_hangup() already skips uart_change_pm(PM_OFF) for consoles;
+	 * apply the same guard here.
+	 */
+	if (!uart_console(port))
+		serial_base_port_set_tx(port, port_dev, false);
 }

 static DEFINE_RUNTIME_DEV_PM_OPS(serial_port_pm,
